# Neo Learn Phase Distortion parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.9). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnPhaseDistortion
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnPd
class NeoLearnPhaseDistortionMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching phase-distortion synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A cosine read through a bent phase (six read geometries: saw, square, narrow pulse, double sine, saw-pulse, trapezoid) whose bend decays on each note, a hard-synced resonant window, a ring modulator and a warm chorus, with an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for rubbery basses, digital plucks, glassy keys and screaming sweeps, or to learn how bending the phase of a sine makes harmonics.

group Core
PhaseBend        "Phase Bend" 0 1000 400 pct
    id phase_bend
    how Bends the speed at which each cycle reads a cosine: 0% reads it evenly (a pure sine), 100% reads part of the cycle much faster than the rest.
    sound Acts like a low-pass filter cutoff without using a filter—opening from a pure, round sine into a sharp, buzzy wave.

Resonance        "Resonance" 0 1000 250 pct
    id resonance
    how Multiplies the frequency of a hard-synced cosine window inside the single-cycle phase reset.
    sound Produces the unmistakable, vocal, screaming 1980s digital filter sweep resonance.

PdWaveShape      "PD Wave" 0 5 0 enum Sawtooth Square Narrow_Pulse Double_Sine Saw_Pulse Trapezoid
    id pd_wave_shape
    how Selects the phase-read geometry (`Sawtooth`, `Square`, `Narrow Pulse`, `Double Sine`, `Saw-Pulse`, `Trapezoid`).
    sound Sets the fundamental harmonic character that emerges as Phase Bend is turned up.

BendDecay        "Bend Decay" 0 1000 520 time 0.01 4
    id bend_decay
    how Sets the decay speed of the dedicated envelope modulating `phase_bend` on each note trigger.
    sound Creates punchy, rubbery 80s synth basses and bright digital plucks that warm up as they sustain.

RingMod          "Ring Mod" 0 1000 0 pct
    id ring_mod
    how Multiplies the primary phase-distorted wave with a secondary carrier oscillator.
    sound Adds clangorous, bell-like, and harmonically complex retro digital overtones.

Chorus           "Chorus" 0 1000 300 pct
    id chorus
    how Engages a warm, slightly noisy bucket-brigade stereo delay chorus on the output.
    sound Widens dry digital waveforms into lush, nostalgic 80s synth keys and pads.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 150 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 520 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 700 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 450 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 573 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnPhaseDistortionMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
